  "security_implications": "In unmasked mode, key_init_cipher[0] XORs two key shares, exposing the plain key and enabling SCA extraction. In masked mode, state_out unmasking is incomplete in this chunk, potentially leaving output data unprotected or undriven. The alert_fatal_o-to-alert_fatal_i feedback loop may affect fault recovery or create persistent alerts. cfg_valid_i is tied to ~ctrl_err_storage; if used functionally, it blocks config during error, but the comment suggests assertion-only usage, which could be a security bypass. Parameters SecAllowForcingMasks and SecSkipPRNGReseeding can weaken masking if misapplied.",
